                <pb facs="0232" n="224" sameAs="frus:frus1941v04/pg224"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.94/2122a: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Ambassador in Japan</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Grew</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1941-05-24T23:00:00-04:00">May 24, 1941—11
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>297. For the Ambassador and Counselor only. Reference a strictly confidential
                    letter of May 2 from an officer of the Department with five enclosures.</p>
                <list>
                    <label>1.</label>
                    <item>On an assumption that it should develop that a satisfactory formula
                        containing mutually acceptable pledges and assurances can be worked out,
                        what is your judgment, given the present situation in Japan and in the
                        world, as to (<hi rendition="#italic">a</hi>) the likelihood that any
                        government in Japan could carry out commitments of the character under
                        reference and (<hi rendition="#italic">b</hi>) the likelihood that the
                        Japanese Government would in good faith do so? Also, your opinion as to
                        advisability of this Government making such commitment?</item>
                    <label>2.</label>
                    <item>Your reply should be as “blind” as may be practicable without risk of
                        misunderstanding.</item>
                </list>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
